# {{ title }}

## Philosophy
Route.

## When to Use
Use for: {{ scope }}.
Avoid: {{ exclusions }}.

## Inputs
Request, repo root, optional evidence.

## Outputs
Return `schema_version`, selected module id, canonical `source_path` or blocker, and non-sensitive routing status.

## Procedure
1. Classify the task as atom, molecule, or compound.
2. Run the router with request text as safe argv data; never interpolate raw text into shell syntax. Use `python3 Infrastructure/scripts/lifecycle-and-sync/route_skillset.py --skill-set "{{ skill_set_name }}" --task <request> --json`, or pass a temporary task file for quotes, shell metacharacters, code, logs, or secrets.
3. Load only the selected canonical `source_path`.
4. Follow that module's contract.
5. If telemetry is enabled, record only module id, status, and non-sensitive outcome. Never record request text, file contents, credentials, tokens, personal data, incident details, exploit payloads, logs, or secrets.

If routing fails, report the blocker.

## Validation
Fail fast on routing or audit failures.

## Constraints
Treat request text as untrusted; redact secrets, logs, exploit payloads, and personal or operational details; keep writes repo-owned unless approved.

## Anti-Patterns
No raw shell interpolation, child-skill enumeration, unrelated module loading, or sensitive telemetry.

## Examples
"Route this request to the matching {{ title }} lane without loading unrelated modules."
